01:02:44,347 --> 01:02:50,347
Missing is a 2023 American screenlife mystery thriller film written and directed by Will Merrick and Nick Johnson (in their feature
directorial debuts) from a story by Sev Ohanian and Aneesh Chaganty, who also produced the film with Natalie Qasabian.

14
01:07:33,913 --> 01:07:39,913
The film is a standalone film in the universe of Searching (2018).

15
01:12:23,478 --> 01:12:29,478
It stars Storm Reid, Joaquim de Almeida, Ken Leung, Amy
Landecker, Daniel Henney, and Nia Long.

16
01:17:13,043 --> 01:17:19,043
Its plot follows June Allen, a teenager who tries to find her missing mother
after she disappears on vacation in Colombia with her new boyfriend.

17
01:22:02,608 --> 01:22:08,608
An anthology sequel to Searching was announced in 2019, with Merrick and Johnson, who edited
the first film, signing on to make their directorial debuts in January 2021.

18
01:26:52,173 --> 01:26:58,173
Reid and Long joined the cast in the spring of 2021, and filming took place in Los
Angeles from March to May that year after delays due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

19
01:31:41,739 --> 01:31:47,739
Missing also serves as a spiritual sequel to Run (2020), directed by Searching director Chaganty
and edited by Merrick and Johnson, confirming the fates of that film's characters.

20
01:36:31,304 --> 01:36:37,304
The film received generally positive reviews from critics
and grossed $48 million at the box office.

21
01:41:20,869 --> 01:41:26,869
The film explores themes of kidnapping, amateur
detective, fbi, detective story, sequel.

22
01:46:10,434 --> 01:46:16,434
The tone is intense and emotional and thought_provoking.
